---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---
<Base title="Couples counselling" description="Couples counselling in Victoria, BC and by secure video across BC with Rachel Glover, RCC. Free 15-minute consultation.">
<div class="wrap"><section class="pg-hero">
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="eyebrow rise" style="--d:.1s">Couples counselling</p>
        <h1 class="b-h1"><span class="mask"><span style="--d:.2s">Feel like a team</span></span><span class="mask acc"><span style="--d:.36s">again.</span></span></h1>
        <p class="lede rise" style="--d:.65s">Every couple wants to feel close, and every couple has differences that create conflict. I help you understand the patterns between you and practise better ways through them, together.</p>
        <div class="rise" style="--d:.8s;display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn" href={site.bookingUrl}>Book a free 15-minute call <span class="arr">→</span></a></div>
      </div>
      <svg class="pg-forms" viewBox="0 0 116 80" aria-hidden="true"><g class="l"><circle cx="40" cy="40" r="36" fill="#CDB792"/></g>
        <circle class="mid" cx="76" cy="40" r="36" clip-path="url(#clipB)" fill="#5C1A26"/>
        <g class="r"><circle cx="76" cy="40" r="35.3" fill="none" stroke="#5C1A26" stroke-width="1.4"/></g></svg>
    </section></div><section class="band"><div class="wrap split2">
      <div class="reveal"><p class="eyebrow">Is this you?</p><h2 class="b-h1 h2">Couples often come to me when…</h2></div>
      <div class="reveal"><ul class="checks stagger"><li>The same argument keeps happening, just with a different topic.</li><li>You feel more like roommates or co-managers than partners.</li><li>Trust has been shaken and you want to rebuild it.</li><li>A big change (a baby, a move, a loss, retirement) has knocked you off balance.</li><li>One of you wants to talk more and the other wants to talk less.</li><li>You’re doing fine, and want to stay that way before committing further.</li></ul></div>
    </div></section><section class="band alt"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="reveal" style="max-width:720px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px"><p class="eyebrow">How we’ll work</p><h2 class="b-h1 h2">Practical sessions, with both of you heard.</h2></div>
      <div class="b1-steps stagger">
        <div class="b1-step"><span class="n">FIRST</span><h3>Understand what’s happening</h3><p class="body">We map out the pattern you get caught in, and what each of you needs that isn’t getting through.</p></div>
        <div class="b1-step"><span class="n">THEN</span><h3>Change how it goes</h3><p class="body">We slow conflict down in the room and practise new ways to raise things, listen and repair.</p></div>
        <div class="b1-step"><span class="n">BETWEEN SESSIONS</span><h3>Try it at home</h3><p class="body">You’ll leave with something concrete to try, and we build on what happened next time.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="band"><div class="wrap a1-fees">
      <div class="reveal"><p class="eyebrow">Session lengths</p><h2 class="b-h1 h2" style="margin-top:16px">Why I recommend 75 minutes.</h2><p class="body" style="margin-top:20px">Couples sessions need time for both people to settle in and be heard. Most couples find 75 minutes gives enough room to get somewhere without feeling rushed.</p></div>
      <ul class="fee-list stagger"><li><span class="what">Couples session</span><span class="len">60 min</span><span class="amt">$180</span></li>
<li><span class="what">Couples session <span class="rec">Recommended</span></span><span class="len">75 min</span><span class="amt">$225</span></li>
<li><span class="what">Couples session</span><span class="len">90 min</span><span class="amt">$270</span></li>
</ul>
    </div></section><section class="band alt"><div class="wrap split2">
      <div class="reveal"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2 class="b-h1 h2">Before you book</h2></div>
      <div class="reveal"><div class="faq reveal"><details><summary>Do we both need to come to every session?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>Usually, yes. Occasionally I’ll suggest a one-to-one session with each of you early on, so I can understand both sides.</p></details><details><summary>What if my partner isn’t sure about counselling?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>That’s common. Book the free 15-minute call together if you can, so they can ask questions and get a feel for how I work.</p></details><details><summary>Is it in person or online?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>Both. Sessions are at my office at 941 Kings Rd in Victoria, or by secure video anywhere in BC.</p></details><details><summary>How many sessions will we need?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><p>It depends on what you’re working on. We’ll talk about it in the first session and check in on progress as we go.</p></details></div></div>
    </div></section><section class="band dark"><div class="wrap b1-close reveal">
      <h2 class="b-h1">Ready to talk? <span>The first call is free.</span></h2>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn light-fill" href={site.bookingUrl}>Book a free consultation <span class="arr">→</span></a><a class="btn ghost" href="/contact#qform">Ask a question</a></div>
    </div></section>
</Base>
